<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the Mac app may do. It is NOT sandboxed, as the Tauri Mac app is not (tauri/src-tauri/Entitlements.plist;
  Matt, 2026-10-09: "un sandbox it"): it keeps its files in its own folder under ~/Library/Application Support,
  reaches a folder or a drive the person chose by its plain path, and needs no entitlement for the network.

  device.audio-input: the microphone, only while a take or a meeting is recorded (macos/Runner/MicChannel.swift).
    A signed release runs under the hardened runtime, where the microphone is closed until this says otherwise:
    without it there is no prompt, and a recording of silence with no error to say why.
  cs.allow-jit and cs.disable-library-validation: a debug build's only, for Dart's own machine and for the ad hoc
    signatures of a debug build's frameworks, should one ever be run hardened.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
